{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he divines divination with it.</b> Do you not have to know — that is why he left it on the table and averted his eyes from it, in order to test you to see whether you would steal it. And one may say, <b>and he divines divination with it</b> — do you not have to know that he will inquire of diviners on its account, for a man like him has diviners who know how to reveal thefts. And he explained <b>with it</b> — on its account. Another interpretation: it is the language of a sign, and its parallel is ״נחשתי ויברכני״ — it seemed to him a bad omen when a precious vessel like it was lost from him. And one should not interpret it as the language of sorcery, for it is unseemly regarding a great man."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:34.722054437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}